        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-06T16:56:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what if the message doesn\u0027t fill up the RX buffer and we detect the end before that. What prevents us from through everything away in reset_rx_fifo?\n\nIs there a high water mark and minimum size in the fifo that we can get an interrupt for after X bytes (and RX fifo isn\u0027t full already)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 249,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 249,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "8c73ad252fff754a8e16520260566e36944adad8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea2eb39e_f7fc78ee",
        "filename": "chip/it83xx/spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 1273969
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-09T10:44:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SPI handshake procedure is slave received data from host and responded to the host after processing. The host will get a corresponding response first before end detection. So if the end is detected when the Rx FIFO is not full, this transaction will abort. \n\nWe will wait the data until Rx FIFO full then to process because Rx FIFO does not receive the data when the CPU starts accessing FIFO after receiving X bytes data. This will lead to error in receiving the next X bytes data.",
      "parentUuid": "3655200a_b49917b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 249,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 249,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "8c73ad252fff754a8e16520260566e36944adad8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
