      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-09T18:49:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am still not understanding. We also need some of this information in the comments here too.\n\n - There is a limitation that the RX fifo stops receiving data asynchronously (or starts dropping data) when the CPU access the fifo (so setting IT83XX_SPI_TXRXFAR?)? We need to document that behavior here\n - What is setting RX fifo to full if the bytes sent from the host is only 20 bytes. That is not enough data to fill the 128 bytes RX fifo?",
      "parentUuid": "ea2eb39e_f7fc78ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 249,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 249,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "8c73ad252fff754a8e16520260566e36944adad8",
